    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **265 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to the new v2 spec and made the whole test suite pass.\n\n### What changed\n\n**New shared helper \u2014 `mapper/OwnerIdentity.java`** (new file)\n- `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` \u2192 full lower-case hex **SHA-256** over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (email trimmed/lower-cased, null components become empty).\n- `soundex(name)` \u2192 standard American Soundex (first letter + 3 digits, `h`/`w` transparent, vowels resetting), used both in the key and the soft-match.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `identityKey` DTO expression now delegates to `OwnerIdentity.identityKey(...)` instead of the old `telephone|email|householdId` concatenation.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Duplicate detection (409) now compares the new SHA-256 identity key, still skipping `deleted` owners and still applying the email-domain blocklist first (that 400 path runs before the key check). `householdId` is no longer part of the key, so the household-based hard-duplicate 409 is gone.\n- `applyPossibleDuplicate` (soft match) now triggers when **`soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match but the `identityKey` differs** (also skips deleted owners for consistency). Same last name + postcode + different telephone \u2192 different key \u2192 created and flagged as a soft match rather than rejected.\n- Removed the now-dead private `identityKey(...)` and `emailForKey(...)` helpers. `householdId` computation is kept (still used for membership sizing).\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions/example to the new spec.\n\n**Tests**\n- `createOwnerIdentityKeyCollisionReturnsConflict` asserted the old plaintext key `\"+16085550120||\"` and relied on same-telephone/different-lastName colliding \u2014 impossible under the new key. Rewrote it to assert a 64-hex key and to use a same-soundex last name for the collision.\n- Added `createOwnerSameHouseholdDifferentTelephoneIsSoftMatchNotConflict` covering the new behaviour: same last name + postcode, different telephone \u2192 201 with `possibleDuplicate: true`.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` v2 spec (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`, `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 which previously failed against the old code \u2014 now passes.",
